{"step_index":965,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-25T03:00:30Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-24T22:00:30-05:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-24T22:00:30-05:00\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/<user>/Downloads/GTA6.Xbox.v1.0.2.1-CYBERLEEK/work/text/mission_text_report.txt`\nTotal Lines: 374\nTotal Bytes: 47435\nShowing lines 1 to 45\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: == missions_chapter_1\r\n2:    0 INT_PROLO              'Prologue'\r\n3:        PROG_INT_PROLO_DESC_REPLAY: Lucia meets with a prison counselor to discuss her arrest and the possibility of early release.\r\n4:        INT_PROLO_DESC: Attend an appointment with your new prison counselor.\r\n5:    1 INT_CHASE              'Gone Fishing'\r\n6:        PROG_INT_CHASE_DESC_REPLAY: When a smuggling run goes bad, Jason has to rescue Donnie from the Kingfishers in Pelican Valley. He returns to his house in the Keys where Lucia calls him and tells him she will be released early.\r\n7:        INT_CHASE_DESC: Help Donnie skim some bricks off a shipment.\r\n8:    2 FT_AMUCO               'Gear Up' (label PROG_FT_AMUCO; own-ID text: 'Gear Up')\r\n9:        PROG_FT_AMUCO: Gear Up\r\n10:        PROG_FT_AMUCO_DESC_REPLAY: Jason heads to his local Ammu-Nation to pick up a longarm gun.\r\n11:    3 FT_KMODSHP             'Just a Scratch' (label PROG_FT_KMODSHP; own-ID text: 'Just a Scratch')\r\n12:        PROG_FT_KMODSHP: Just a Scratch\r\n13:        PROG_FT_KMODSHP_DESC_REPLAY: Jason takes his Ganado to Joey at Coastal Auto Care for some much-needed repairs.\r\n14:    4 COM_KBOS_SHOP          'Lab Fees'\r\n15:        PROG_COM_KBOS_SHOP_DESC_REPLAY: Jason heads to a gift shop (that's a front for an acid lab) to collect rent for Brian. They have no money, so Jason takes product instead.\r\n16:        COM_KBOS_SHOP_DESC: Visit The Boutique to collect for Brian.\r\n17:    5 COM_KBOS_COLAT         'Unwanted Attention'\r\n18:        PROG_COM_KBOS_COLAT_DESC_REPLAY: Cal and Jason drive to Ham\n<truncated 1617 bytes>\noming Home'\r\n33:        PROG_INT_PRISO_DESC_REPLAY: When Lucia is released from prison, Jason takes her to the Rusty Anchor to celebrate with some friends. Lucia's old cellmate Kat arrives with her rich boyfriend, Mattia. Lucia wants Jason to work with Mattia, but a fight breaks up their evening. Jason and Lucia go home to bed.\r\n34:        INT_PRISO_DESC: With Lucia out of prison, it's time to catch up.\r\n35:   11 INT_BANK               'Buck Me'\r\n36:        PROG_INT_BANK_DESC_REPLAY: Jason and Lucia attempt to set up a joint bank account, but their credit isn't good enough. They end up with the BuckMe app instead.\r\n37:        INT_BANK_DESC: Open up a bank account with Lucia.\r\n38:   12 CTI_PIL_RD_SH          'Clean Up After Donnie' (label CTI_PIL_RD_BC_PARENT; own-ID text: \"Find Donnie's Package\")\r\n39:        PROG_CTI_PIL_RD_SH_DESC_REPLAY: Jason heads to the swamps to recover a drug package mislaid by Donnie.\r\n40:        CTI_PIL_RD_SH_DESC: One of the packages from Donnie's botched delivery is sending a signal near a fishing spot in Hamlet.\r\n41:   13 COM_KBOS_PLNDATE       'Down to Earth'\r\n42:        PROG_COM_KBOS_PLNDATE_DESC_REPLAY: Jason takes Lucia on a smuggling run in Brian's seaplane, but they run into trouble with the Brian's new suppliers. After dropping off the packages from the plane, Lucia realizes she's missed calls from her P.O. She and Jason get back home just in time.\r\n43:        COM_KBOS_PLNDATE_DESC: Take Brian's seaplane and pick up his package, then deliver the contents to his buyers.\r\n44:   14 INT_PLNSH              'Clear Skies'\r\n45:        PROG_INT_PLNSH_DESC_REPLAY: After escorting a smuggler plane into Leonida under the radar for Brian, Donnie convinces Jason to make an unscheduled stop so he can sell some stolen product to a local biker gang. Donnie's plan goes badly wrong but Jason gets them out alive.\r\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
